# Build scratch. Every paper's LaTeX source is kept in paper-sources/, banded by rank, so the
# build tree itself is regenerable working state and is not stored: it held 35 660 files,
# including a duplicate PDF of every paper and LaTeX's .aux/.out droppings.
engine/build/
engine/build_*/
engine/papers-ranked/

# The `was`-keyed master. The same PDFs as papers/ under different names; restore_master.py
# rebuilds it exactly from papers/ and rank-map.json, verified byte for byte.
engine/papers-old-numbering/

# Downloaded OEIS b-files. A cache, refetchable, 145 MB.
engine/bcache/

# NO ZIP ARCHIVES. The papers live in papers/, one PDF per result, and nothing bundles them.
# The pattern used to name one archive; a 7.2 MB truncated zip of papers 1030-1074 sat in
# engine/ under a scrambled name for a week because it did not match. Every archive is ignored
# now, whatever it is called.
conjecture-papers-*.zip
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

*.log
*.pids
*.bak
__pycache__/

# The sweep's lock file: transient runtime state naming a live process, meaningless in a
# checkout. It exists because two sweeps writing one results file silently destroy each
# other's proved results, which happened once and left no trace but the count.
engine/*.json.lock
# Every sweep shard's working files, whatever TAG they run under. shard_* covered only the
# untagged run, so a tagged one left its transient state in the repository.
engine/shard*_hits_*.json
engine/shard*_done_*.json
engine/shard*_caps_*.json
engine/shard_*.json

# The independent checks' per-entry progress files. Each is rewritten after every entry, so
# while a run is going the working tree is dirty every few seconds and no commit of one is
# ever current. They are progress, not results: the result is the summary each run writes
# once it has nothing left to attempt, in engine/deep-check/indep-*.json, and that is stored.
engine/indep*_done.json
